Subject: wifi: ath11k: initialize and detach NSS mesh dump ownership

Initialize the radio's NSS dump lock with the radio object, before it is
published. Unlike pdev setup, allocation is skipped for an already
registered radio during recovery, so this does not reinitialize a lock
that may still have users. Keep the NSS-disabled configuration buildable.

Detach stale mesh-path entries with list_splice_tail_init() before freeing
them outside the lock. list_splice_tail() leaves the reusable source head
pointing at entries that the request then frees, including on TX failure.
The next reply or request must see an empty, valid source head instead.

This repairs conditional mesh dump ownership, not NSS control teardown,
firmware DMA quiescence, concurrent dump transactions or stock throughput.
The current AX6 stock configuration does not enable NSS mesh support.

Upstream-Status: Pending

---

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
@@ -11300,3 +11300,6 @@ int ath11k_mac_allocate(struct ath11k_base *ab)
 		ar->num_rx_chains = get_num_chains(pdev->cap.rx_chain_mask);
 
+#ifdef CPTCFG_ATH11K_NSS_SUPPORT
+		spin_lock_init(&ar->nss.dump_lock);
+#endif
 		pdev->ar = ar;
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
@@ -1833,3 +1833,3 @@ int ath11k_nss_dump_mpath_request(struct ath11k_vif *arvif)
 	spin_lock_bh(&ar->nss.dump_lock);
-	list_splice_tail(&nss->mpath_dump, &local_entry);
+	list_splice_tail_init(&nss->mpath_dump, &local_entry);
 	arvif->nss.mpath_dump_num_entries = 0;
